{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command Aaron — this is the torah of the burnt offering.</b> After he has set forth the making of the offerings, he states the torah befitting each and every one, in which he alludes to a contemplative element in them. And there is no doubt that there is great distinction among the children of the living El in their actions and intentions, likened to the distinction among the kinds of offerings. And concerning the burnt offering he notes that all of it is upon the altar for a pleasing fragrance; yet part of it is a true burnt offering in the flame of the altar, and he says that this is the burnt offering in truth. And part of it is beside the altar, namely the ashes, which retain some fatness, so that the fire burns in it together with that part that is the true burnt offering, as it says: <b>the ashes which the fire consumes of the burnt offering</b>. And part of it, namely the fully consumed ashes, they remove outside the camp in lesser garments — from wherever its removal may be, to a pure place."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:54.112587448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}